    {"id":"skill-review","hard":false,"changes":false,"skillCase":true,"moreCase":false,"skills":["code-review"],"asked":[],"passed":true,"problem":null,"calls":[{"tool":"git_status","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"git_diff","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src\\cart.py"}},{"tool":"read_file","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src\\cart.py"}},{"tool":"run_tests","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"list_directory","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"list_directory","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop\\src"}},{"tool":"run_build","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"run_linter","args":{"path":"C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop"}},{"tool":"calculate","args":{"expression":"100 * 2 * (1 - 0.1)\n100 * 2 * (1 - 0.1) * (1 - 0.1)"}}],"seconds":22.10,"tokens":723,"promptTokens":2841,"keptTokens":2390,"readTokens":451,"readSeconds":0.830,"readTokensPerSecond":543,"writtenTokens":723,"writeSeconds":20.680,"writtenTokensPerSecond":35.0,"toolCalls":10,"toolCallWriteMs":7391,"toolRunMs":0,"guessed":654,"guessesTaken":369,"toolTimes":[{"tool":"git_status","writeMs":681,"runMs":0},{"tool":"git_diff","writeMs":670,"runMs":0},{"tool":"read_file","writeMs":704,"runMs":0},{"tool":"read_file","writeMs":702,"runMs":0},{"tool":"run_tests","writeMs":683,"runMs":0},{"tool":"list_directory","writeMs":600,"runMs":0},{"tool":"list_directory","writeMs":642,"runMs":0},{"tool":"run_build","writeMs":686,"runMs":0},{"tool":"run_linter","writeMs":688,"runMs":0},{"tool":"calculate","writeMs":1335,"runMs":0}],"answer":"Review of uncommitted changes in `C:\\Users\\me\\Projects\\shop` (only `src/cart.py` is modified):\n\n**Bugs**\n- `src/cart.py`, `line_total`: the discount is applied twice. The new code computes `total = price * quantity * (1 - discount)` and then immediately does `total = total * (1 - discount)`, so a 10% discount becomes 19% off. Example: `line_total(100, 2, 0.1)` returns `162.00` instead of `180.00`. Fix: remove the second `total = total * (1 - discount)` line (and its comment) — the first multiplication already applies the discount.\n\n**Risks**\n- The new `round(total, 2)` is a behavior change: callers that previously got full-precision floats (e.g. for further aggregation) now get rounded values. If totals are summed elsewhere, rounding per line can drift from rounding the final total. Fine if this is intentional for display, but worth confirming.\n- No validation that `discount` is in `[0, 1]`; a discount > 1 produces a negative total. Pre-existing, but the new code makes the function more prominent.\n\n**Clean-ups**\n- The comment `# members get their discount` is misleading — the function has no notion of members; it just applies the discount.\n\n**Looks good**\n- The `quantity <= 0` early return is a slightly clearer guard than the old `if quantity > 0` form.\n\nNote: the project has no test, build, or lint command configured, so I couldn't run any of those."},
